Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
madame  during the past 70 years the president  of the french republic has relied on  very few constants at the international  level  times have changed  europe has evolved our continent is  again experiencing war  throughout these transformations your  devotion to our alliance and to our  friendship has remained and has helped  build trust that brought freedom and  prosperity to our continent since your  first state visit to france when you  were welcomed to paris by a generation  who alongside your army navy and air  force had fought for the freedom we now  enjoy  you have visited us many times  you have shared our joys  and seen the deep affection and  admiration that the people of france  have for you you have also visited the  graves where so many of your young men  lie  and since the respect and honor we  constantly pay to those who sent from  your homes to protect ours  you are the golden thread that binds our  two countries the proof of the  unwavering friendship between our  nations your first toast to one of my  predecessors rene koti reminded us that  trust and understanding should endure  forever  your words were matched by a lifetime of  devotion to our alliance  from the dark days when your family  welcomed general the girl in your home  to his joy to welcome you in his you  have been a constant presence and a  source of wisdom  for the leaders of our two countries  this year  the 70s of your reign we celebrate your  achievements  we are grateful for your courage and we  share the respect and love  that british people and commonwealth  have always shown you

